      <activity id="7da84849-a161-57c4-98bc-6d72660fe6b4" activityNameId="2b076a78-4366-590d-ad55-f5ff13a2011c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Monochloropentafluoroethane, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Monochloropentafluoroethane, at plant
The multioutput-process "ethylene chlorofluorination" delivers the co-products monochloropentafluoroethane and hexafluoroethane. The allocation is based on stoechiometric calculation.;
UUID: 457e88a1-b4f0-31cc-af30-bd5ffa948cb1
Chlorofluorination of ethylene including materials, energy uses, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled for the world..
Technology: Chlorofluorination of ethylene 
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Energy consumptions and emissions are estimated. Infrastructure and transports are calculated with standard values.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_457e88a1-b4f0-31cc-af30-bd5ffa948cb1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
